This week was pretty chill, and imma start things out with a note before we
jump in. Ever since this last transfer started I've had some pretty awful
anxious feelings in the mornings. Its like theres a big weight Suspended
over me. I've prayed about this earnestly and the last couple days
(Saturday and Sunday) I've felt much better. If things are still feeling
really bad I will consult one of the mission Health people about it, but I
want to say that God Hears our prayers and eases our burdens according to
our faith and willingness. I know that he loves each and every one of you.

Tuesday
Today we decided to try and visit a member and then do housing nearby. On
the bike ride to the lady's house, we were Riding along the side of the
road when My companion (in front of me) suddenly swerved to the left to go
behind a guarding rail. I didn=E2=80=99t have enough time to go after him, =
and I
obviously couldn't swerve to the right or I'd get hit by a car, so I tried
going left and my tires skidded and my Knee went straight into the divider
=F0=9F=91=80 luckily It was like sheet metal and kind of curved, but it was=
 still a
big impact. My knee was OK but pretty banged up. (I made a little sketch of
what I ran into) Anyways we kept going to the member=E2=80=99s place, and s=
he was
actually home! It turns out she showed up to our Eikaiwa last Saturday not
knowing it was canceled =F0=9F=98=B1 I hope not a lot of people showed up =
=F0=9F=92=80 anyways
she was super sweet and I don't think their family has been to church in a
little while, and she seemed a bit hesitant talking with us. She is going
to a stake beach cleaning thing This next Saturday though, which is great!
We unfortunately can=E2=80=99t go because of Eikaiwa but it sounds like a g=
ood
opportunity! After visiting this lady, we started to walk around and do a
bit of housing. We found a place to stop our bikes, and went to say hi to a
lady in her front yard. Then the crazy things started happening lol. We
were talking with her about religion and stuff, and she said that its hard
for her to believe there is a God with war going on across the world. She
also told us about how she was one time Working on the flowers in front of
her house, when two Jehovah Witnesses came up and asked what she was doing.
I don=E2=80=99t entirely understand everything she was saying, but I think =
it was
something along the lines of she should just get rid of or kill the injured
flowers? Idk anyways she thought it was pretty mean of them, and she was
even crying about it (and also about seeing war and stuff on TV). Then this
random guy walked by and said Hi, and ended up being a part of the
conversation lol. He lives near the lady (Nao-Chan) and his name is
Jin-Chan. We talked with the two of them for almost an hour out in front of
their house about all kinds of things. Jin-Chan has apparently met with
Missionaries in the past and told us that it is just so much easier and
more comfortable to practice English with Mormons lol. His English is
actually pretty great. Sofoul=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 tried giving a book of Morm=
on to Nao-Chan
before we left, and she basically said because she isn't going to read it,
there's no meaning in the gesture. Hopefully we Can go back and visit again
and maybe she will change her mind =F0=9F=A4=94 Throughout this wild conver=
sation she
also gave us some home-dried and flavored seaweed, as well as some cool
citrus drinks. What a sick lady. Before Jin-Chan left he told us that we
can talk again if we see him around that area, and Nao-Chan is ok with us
coming back to visit her. Around the end of our wild conversation we also
got to meet Nao-Chan's husband, who was getting ready to head to work. He
was also super nice, it would be cool if we can meet with them again.
Anyways, after that we headed over to the seaside to try and find somewhere
I could sit down for a little bit. We saw two fishermen sitting by a shed,
and asked if they knew of a place to sit nearby, and they offered that we
go and sit down with them =F0=9F=98=82 We were talking with the two guys wh=
en another
one showed up and one of the first two left. Definitely a bizarre
interaction but it's cool to meet with people in all circumstances of life.
The original Fisherman that stayed talked about some wild stuff but also
invited us to a place where everyone that comes can have a meal for free.
It happened to be the very next day, so we agreed to go! (Also it's a once
a month event so it's pretty awesome we met the guy right then) we
eventually had to leave but it was cool talking =F0=9F=98=86 We ended off t=
he day by
heading to the church to practice guitar with Shiko which was fun as usual.

Wednesday
Today we had a bit of time for streeting around Ozaki and talked with a
sweet Old Lady. She said that walking around the block and talking with Old
people like her was doing a public service lol. She was very kind. We also
took some time to write some more note cards that we can leave in Mailboxes
as we house. I always try to write every one differently, so I=E2=80=99m no=
t super
fast lol. I believe that this Extra effort might be what someone needs to
see to make the step and call our number. Today we visited the art store
again and talked for a while with Watanabe=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 and one of her=
 friends who
teaches a bunch of art classes. Elder Sofoul and I shared a bunch of cool
photos (from me, art I had made, from him, floral arrangements his
girlfriend had made) with the two of them. I showed them the picture I made
of Jesus's Tomb after his resurrection and explained to them a bit of that
story, it was really neat. They said that even before they knew what the
drawing was that they could feel something looking at it. Maybe I can make
some more gospel art to share with them, it seems like a good way to
connect spiritually. Before Eikaiwa tonight, we tried going to the
=E2=80=9Ceveryone Eats together=E2=80=9D type place that the two fishermen =
had recommended.
It was so awesome! It was mostly kids that were serving food around to a
bunch of people in a big pavilion. We both got given a tray of food, and it
was actually really good. We talked with two ladies and they both are going
to come to our Eikaiwa, and also likely bring their kids! They exchanges
Lines with us too =F0=9F=98=8E. We also saw one of the Fishermen that we me=
t before
and Said Hi to him, and I somehow got him to exchange Line info with me
too, even though he didn't understand how his phone really worked at all
lol. It was sick. He texted me a few days later and invited us to the next
two events, over the next two months. Super awesome. Afterwards we hurried
back to the Church to set up for Eikaiwa as well as play ping pong with
Yasueda=E3=81=95=E3=82=93=E3=80=81one of our regulars At Eikaiwa. Eikaiwa w=
ent well, and after that
we headed back to the apartment for the night.

Thursday
Today was awesome! We had a chance to meet with a returned missionary,
Pentreath=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81, at the Bishop's House! It was super chill talk=
ing with him,
especially considering we were actually disappointed when we realized we
couldn't ask him about friends in the area because he went home, but we
unexpectedly got a chance to talk with him and got a lot of good info!! The
food was great as usual, and I again had to be very cautious not to make
myself throw up lol. We spent some time today also contacting some Grey
dots and one of them said he'd like to meet up with us for a lesson! We
will meet with him next week =F0=9F=99=8F Today was also SKK (weekly planni=
ng) and we
got a good chance to talk about or friends and what we wanna do with the
area. Good times. Lastly we had a super cool lesson with Yasueda=E3=81=95=
=E3=82=93 and
Dono=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 joining us to help share her experiences. We talked =
about the book
of Mormon and a bit about the Godhead. Yasueda=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 doesn't wa=
nt to join our
church but maybe her heart will open as she continues to hear our Lessons
and messages. We also played a bit of ping pong together too =F0=9F=98=86

Friday and Saturday
Friday was a district leader meeting in Kobe, and during that time I got to
have mini exchanges with Pistorius=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81. He's a super humble E=
lder, I vibe
with him. We did some studies in a park whilst getting assailed by
mosquitos, and tried a bit of streeting. We only really talked with one
cool old dude but he was very friendly and probably has a good impression
of the missionaries now which is great. After that we went to meet Up with
one of the Elders=E2=80=99 Friends =E2=80=9CLime.=E2=80=9D his name probabl=
y doesn't mean lime but
you pronounced it like that so it's kinda cool. He's big into fashion. We
went to Denny's With him, and Denny's is lowkey a super boujee restaurant
in Japan. It was kinda pricey and it had fancy music playing lol. Pretty
chill mini exchange. The next day we met 4 chill lads at a park and danced
with them. I also tripped and fell into one of their bikes and lost aura =
=F0=9F=98=AD
We gave them each a flyer to our Eikaiwa and they followed Sofoul=E9=95=B7=
=E8=80=81=E2=80=99s
Instagram =F0=9F=98=8E Today we did a bunch of housing as well, it wasn't s=
uper
effective but it feels great to be doing so much each day. Saturday morning
was also Eikaiwa, and 5 new people came!!! Super awesome. It was kind of
awkward and mostly just introducing the class but it was so fire to have
more people there. Afterwards we went to KFC so Sofoul=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 co=
uld get a free
biscuit with a coupon. Later we went to Panda Express and went to the Lego
store (to say hi to someone who works there that we met before, not so that
Elder Sofoul could buy a lego F1 car) and even got to say hi to Lime who
actually worked nearby =F0=9F=98=82 Good times

Sunday
Today was Fast and Testimony meeting, and it was a good spiritual time.
During Second hour I made some cool art in our lesson I will attach a photo
=F0=9F=93=B8 after that we had our Missionary work coordination meeting, wh=
ich was
great. We got to talk about the huge success with Eikaiwa, how we attempted
visiting members, and also made some plans to visit more members with
members =F0=9F=98=86 throughout these things were also followups with the d=
istrict
and cleaning of the apartment, which is almost to the point where its
probably the mission's cleanest apartment, its getting there. Later we met
back up at the church to have a dinnereon (luncheon but later) for the soon
to be Elder Otani. There was a bunch of cool food, and at the end everyone
went around in a circle and gave their final advice to him. It was pretty
sweet to see the impact someone can have in their own ward. All in all,
great Sunday! (Today Bishop also told us about a phrase Less WiFi, More
Nephi. Apparently it means like focus less on your phone and more on being
like Nephi Or reading The Book of Mormon lol)

Pday
For Pday we had a much more laid back series of events than we did last
time with the Barbecue and what not. We visited that one thrift shop I
always visit, Hobby-Off, a home improvement Store, and we did our shopping.
Highlight was definitely calling with my family and playing Boggle. Aside
from Pday stuff, we had an Eikaiwa Video call with Aime, and spent a little
time making Origami We can give to members. Sofoul=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 made a=
n X-wing with
Facebook instructions, it was dope. Not a super crazy Pday, but it was a
good time.

Love you guys so much. I will try and send some time responding to people
this next week, I've been bad about that. I appreciate all That you do for
me.

Elder Killian

--000000000000b1d6a60636d3c425
