ce guitar with Shiko which was fun as usual.</div><div dir=3D"auto"><br></d=
iv><div dir=3D"auto">Wednesday</div><div dir=3D"auto">Today we had a bit of=
 time for streeting around Ozaki and talked with a sweet Old Lady. She said=
 that walking around the block and talking with Old people like her was doi=
ng a public service lol. She was very kind. We also took some time to write=
 some more note cards that we can leave in Mailboxes as we house. I always =
try to write every one differently, so I=E2=80=99m not super fast lol. I be=
lieve that this Extra effort might be what someone needs to see to make the=
 step and call our number. Today we visited the art store again and talked =
for a while with Watanabe=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 and one of her friends who teac=
hes a bunch of art classes. Elder Sofoul and I shared a bunch of cool photo=
s (from me, art I had made, from him, floral arrangements his girlfriend ha=
d made) with the two of them. I showed them the picture I made of Jesus&#39=
;s Tomb after his resurrection and explained to them a bit of that story, i=
t was really neat. They said that even before they knew what the drawing wa=
s that they could feel something looking at it. Maybe I can make some more =
gospel art to share with them, it seems like a good way to connect spiritua=
lly. Before Eikaiwa tonight, we tried going to the =E2=80=9Ceveryone Eats t=
ogether=E2=80=9D type place that the two fishermen had recommended. It was =
so awesome! It was mostly kids that were serving food around to a bunch of =
people in a big pavilion. We both got given a tray of food, and it was actu=
ally really good. We talked with two ladies and they both are going to come=
 to our Eikaiwa, and also likely bring their kids! They exchanges Lines wit=
h us too =F0=9F=98=8E. We also saw one of the Fishermen that we met before =
and Said Hi to him, and I somehow got him to exchange Line info with me too=
, even though he didn&#39;t understand how his phone really worked at all l=
ol. It was sick. He texted me a few days later and invited us to the next t=
wo events, over the next two months. Super awesome. Afterwards we hurried b=
ack to the Church to set up for Eikaiwa as well as play ping pong with Yasu=
eda=E3=81=95=E3=82=93=E3=80=81one of our regulars At Eikaiwa. Eikaiwa went =
well, and after that we headed back to the apartment for the night.</div><d=
iv dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">Thursday</div><div dir=3D"auto"=
>Today was awesome! We had a chance to meet with a returned missionary, Pen=
treath=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81, at the Bishop&#39;s House! It was super chill tal=
king with him,  especially considering we were actually disappointed when w=
e realized we couldn&#39;t ask him about friends in the area because he wen=
t home, but we unexpectedly got a chance to talk with him and got a lot of =
good info!! The food was great as usual, and I again had to be very cautiou=
s not to make myself throw up lol. We spent some time today also contacting=
 some Grey dots and one of them said he&#39;d like to meet up with us for a=
 lesson! We will meet with him next week =F0=9F=99=8F Today was also SKK (w=
eekly planning) and we got a good chance to talk about or friends and what =
we wanna do with the area. Good times. Lastly we had a super cool lesson wi=
th Yasueda=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 and Dono=E5=A7=89=E5=A6=B9 joining us to help =
share her experiences. We talked about the book of Mormon and a bit about t=
he Godhead. Yasueda=E3=81=95=E3=82=93 doesn&#39;t want to join our church b=
ut maybe her heart will open as she continues to hear our Lessons and messa=
ges. We also played a bit of ping pong together too =F0=9F=98=86</div><div =
dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">Friday and Saturday</div><div dir=
=3D"auto">Friday was a district leader meeting in Kobe, and during that tim=
e I got to have mini exchanges with Pistorius=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81. He&#39;s a=
 super humble Elder, I vibe with him. We did some studies in a park whilst =
getting assailed by mosquitos, and tried a bit of streeting. We only really=
 talked with one cool old dude but he was very friendly and probably has a =
good impression of the missionaries now which is great. After that we went =
to meet Up with one of the Elders=E2=80=99 Friends =E2=80=9CLime.=E2=80=9D =
his name probably doesn&#39;t mean lime but you pronounced it like that so =
it&#39;s kinda cool. He&#39;s big into fashion. We went to Denny&#39;s With=
 him, and Denny&#39;s is lowkey a super boujee restaurant in Japan. It was =
kinda pricey and it had fancy music playing lol. Pretty chill mini exchange=
. The next day we met 4 chill lads at a park and danced with them. I also t=
ripped and fell into one of their bikes and lost aura =F0=9F=98=AD We gave =
them each a flyer to our Eikaiwa and they followed Sofoul=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=
=E2=80=99s Instagram =F0=9F=98=8E Today we did a bunch of housing as well, =
it wasn&#39;t super effective but it feels great to be doing so much each d=
ay. Saturday morning was also Eikaiwa, and 5 new people came!!! Super aweso=
me. It was kind of awkward and mostly just introducing the class but it was=
 so fire to have more people there. Afterwards we went to KFC so Sofoul=E9=
=95=B7=E8=80=81 could get a free biscuit with a coupon. Later we went to Pa=
nda Express and went to the Lego store (to say hi to someone who works ther=
e that we met before, not so that Elder Sofoul could buy a lego F1 car) and=
 even got to say hi to Lime who actually worked nearby =F0=9F=98=82 Good ti=
mes</div><div dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">Sunday</div><div dir=
=3D"auto">Today was Fast and Testimony meeting, and it was a good spiritual=
 time. During Second hour I made some cool art in our lesson I will attach =
a photo =F0=9F=93=B8 after that we had our Missionary work coordination mee=
ting, which was great. We got to talk about the huge success with Eikaiwa, =
how we attempted visiting members, and also made some plans to visit more m=
embers with members =F0=9F=98=86 throughout these things were also followup=
s with the district and cleaning of the apartment, which is almost to the p=
oint where its probably the mission&#39;s cleanest apartment, its getting t=
here. Later we met back up at the church to have a dinnereon (luncheon but =
later) for the soon to be Elder Otani. There was a bunch of cool food, and =
at the end everyone went around in a circle and gave their final advice to =
him. It was pretty sweet to see the impact someone can have in their own wa=
rd. All in all, great Sunday! (Today Bishop also told us about a phrase Les=
s WiFi, More Nephi. Apparently it means like focus less on your phone and m=
ore on being like Nephi Or reading The Book of Mormon lol)</div><div dir=3D=
"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">Pday</div><div dir=3D"auto">For Pday we =
had a much more laid back series of events than we did last time with the B=
arbecue and what not. We visited that one thrift shop I always visit, Hobby=
-Off, a home improvement Store, and we did our shopping. Highlight was defi=
nitely calling with my family and playing Boggle. Aside from Pday stuff, we=
 had an Eikaiwa Video call with Aime, and spent a little time making Origam=
i We can give to members. Sofoul=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 made an X-wing with Face=
book instructions, it was dope. Not a super crazy Pday, but it was a good t=
ime.</div><div dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">Love you guys so mu=
ch. I will try and send some time responding to people this next week, I&#3=
9;ve been bad about that. I appreciate all That you do for me.=C2=A0</div><=
div dir=3D"auto"><br></div><div dir=3D"auto">Elder Killian</div></div>

